# GIT / GITHUB WORKFLOW
- Branches: `main` (production, protected), `develop` (integration, protected), `feature/{REQ-ID}-{short-name}`,
  `fix/{short-name}`. Never commit directly to `main` or `develop`.
- Small PRs (< ~400 changed lines), one requirement or sub-feature each. The OTHER developer reviews and approves.
- Commit format (Conventional Commits): `feat(leads): add lead conversion wizard [FR-LEAD-005]`.
- Rebase on `develop` daily (`git pull --rebase origin develop`) and before opening a PR.
- Migrations: prefix timestamps naturally; if two branches add migrations to the same table, coordinate in the PR.
- Shared files (`routes/web.php`, `layouts/app.blade.php`, nav, `bootstrap/app.php`): keep edits minimal, merge quickly.
  Prefer per-module route files (`routes/leads.php`) loaded from `routes/web.php` to avoid conflicts.
- PR checklist: tests pass, Pint clean, policy + validation present, SRS ID referenced, screenshots for UI changes.
- Cursor: use Manual/Auto mode only (never YOLO on `develop`/`main`); commit before every large Composer run so it can be rolled back.
